# Pinned refs of the living-doc components this repository's checks run or read. It is the ONE place to
# bump them. Read by:
#   - tests/collector/collector-gh.sh and tests/collector/toolkit.sh, which source it for both runners,
#     tests/examples/regen-collector-snapshots.sh and tests/testbed/run-testbed-stage.sh
#     (COLLECTOR_GH_REF, TOOLKIT_REF);
#   - tests/examples/check_utilities_pins.py, the living-doc-utilities pin report (every ref);
#   - .github/workflows/retired-names.yml, which clones each component at its ref for
#     tests/docs/retired_names_check.py (every ref);
#   - tests/integration/local-integration.sh, the local integration runner, which clones and runs each component at
#     its ref unless its configuration names a tag or full SHA (every ref).
#
# Bumping a pin is a reviewed change, exactly like a dependency bump. A bump of COLLECTOR_GH_REF or
# TOOLKIT_REF commits the regenerated docs/examples/_expected/** in the same PR
# (see CONTRIBUTING.md -> "Regenerating the collector snapshots") and keeps the testbed stage
# (tests/testbed/run-testbed-stage.sh) green. GENERATOR_MARKDOWN_REF feeds no snapshot and no stage:
# a bump of it alone regenerates nothing. The pin report shows each component's living-doc-utilities
# version, and the snapshot job (.github/workflows/real-collector.yml) fails on a minor skew with the corpus
# checker's (tests/examples/requirements-examples-check.txt), the version tests/examples/examples_check.py checks
# the before/after pairs in docs/guides/authoring-documentation.md and the codes in
# docs/reference/errors.md against.
#
# Refs MUST be a tag or a full commit SHA. A floating branch name (master, main, ...) is not allowed.

# AbsaOSS/living-doc-collector-gh - provides the `doc-source` and `ui-tests` mining modes, and the
# runtime requirements.txt the job builds the collector's venv from.
COLLECTOR_GH_REF=v0.2.0

# AbsaOSS/living-doc-toolkit - provides the `normalize-docs`, `normalize-tests` and `coverage-matrix`
# commands, and the runtime requirements.txt the job builds the toolkit's venv from.
TOOLKIT_REF=v0.1.0

# AbsaOSS/living-doc-generator-markdown - run only by the local integration runner, never by CI: CI's
# pin report reads its runtime requirements.txt, and the retired-names check reads its tracked files.
GENERATOR_MARKDOWN_REF=v0.1.0
